  "cause": "**The projectile came through the roof shortly after midnight and hit the surgery department, and by Thursday afternoon the health ministry in Gaza had a list instead of a building.** At least **six** people were killed at **Nasser hospital** in **Khan Younis** — among them the surgeon **Dr Rizk Abu Shaira**, who had worked at the hospital through the entire war, and a **13-year-old boy** — with at least **a dozen** wounded and parts of the second floor wrecked, according to **AP**, whose video team documented the damage. **Médecins Sans Frontières** condemned *\"another deadly attack\"* on Nasser. The **Israeli military** said it had targeted **a senior Hamas militant and other fighters**, and that it was *\"looking into reports\"* that medical workers — Abu Shaira among them — and patients had been killed: a formulation that concedes the possibility while withholding the finding. **Hamas** called it *\"a heinous crime targeting a civilian medical facility.\"* **Nasser is not a building that can absorb a second strike and remain a hospital.** It was hit by a **double Israeli strike in August 2025** that killed at least **twenty**, including journalists and health workers, and **AP** describes it now as one of the **few remaining functioning medical facilities** in the Strip. A ceasefire has nominally held since **October 2025**; more than **1,620** people have been killed since then according to the territory's health ministry, whose figures the **UN** treats as reliable, against more than **74,650** since October 2023. Israel does not permit international news organisations into Gaza — so the two accounts of what the surgery department was being used for cannot be tested by anyone who is not a party to the war. In the same week **France turned away a settler leader** at its border, one of the first European actions aimed at a named individual rather than a statement. And the political layer is still counting signatures: the **26th Knesset** seats its **Arrangements Committee** under **Roy Folkman**, Speaker **Amir Ohana** has set the vote on his own replacement for **Tuesday 17 November at 4 p.m.** on **67** signatures, **Likud** alleges foreign interference and says Arab-led parties *\"stole\"* the election, the **Shin Bet** chief has made what Israeli reporters call unprecedented allegations, and Justice **Noam Solberg** certified the result. The journalist **Abed Abu Shehadeh**, held five days without charge over an interview published openly on 26 October, was released on **9 November**.",
