   "**\"Looking into reports\" is an investigation assigned to the party that fired, and repetition turns it into a genre** — the IDF says it targeted a Hamas commander and is examining claims about the medics; the health ministry says the ward was a ward; each new strike on a hospital arrives with the same two-sentence structure; the direct effect is that the strike's legality is never decided, only asserted; the compound consequence is that the *form* of denial becomes predictable enough to be discounted in advance — so the fourth or fifth hospital is met with the sentence people already expected, and a legal category that requires case-by-case adjudication dissolves into background noise that no side has to answer",
