  "hinge": "§19:20 makes the account the condition — thoughts and deeds are not free of consequence because they were intended, and *false testimony* is named in the same verse as killing. What is missing in Khan Younis is not condemnation, which is abundant, but an account: a record produced by someone who did not fire and does not govern. That is a signature away. A joint protocol, agreed this month, under which any strike on a health facility is followed within 48 hours by a published record — munition type, trajectory, the floor struck, the function of the rooms, the names and ages of the dead — with **ICRC** or **WHO** access to the site from whichever side holds the ground. Israel says the building was a command post; that is a testable claim and a state with evidence should be the first to want it tested. Hamas says it was a war crime; that is testable too. Neither can be established by a spokesman, and a hospital hit twice in fifteen months has earned the right to a third-party finding. The Knesset can perform the same operation on its own file before 17 November: put the Shin Bet's election material into the Arrangements Committee under a written mandate rather than letting it leak into a partisan dispute, and the house gains the one thing it lacks — a finding it can cite."
