  "hinge": "§10:49 is one sentence and it cuts both ways — a promise carried out is evidence of sincerity, and a promise announced and not carried out is evidence of the opposite. The prisoner exchange is the test case, and it can be completed before the next round convenes: publish the number, publish the list, publish the date, and let the buses run. Three more pages would cost no side a metre of ground. First, Europe names its representative **before** the next round — one person, with a written mandate from the 27, so the seat is filled by a European decision rather than a Russian indulgence. Second, the infrastructure annex: a published joint schedule of protected installations — the refineries struck since late October, the substations and generating plants hit in Ukraine, the ports and the cold chain — with a named verification body and a 30-day reporting cycle, countable and therefore signable. Third, the alumina file: publish what Europe still sells Russia that its own defence industry needs, and the negotiation acquires a subject it can measure. The shuttle produced the word *yes* in Moscow. The remaining work is clerical, and clerical work is what turns a blessing into an agreement."
