  "cause": "**The board resolved the question by removing the man and fixing the structure in the same press release.** On **12 November** Nvidia announced that **Jensen Huang** had resigned as President, Chief Executive Officer and a member of the board, **effective immediately**; that **Colette Kress**, executive vice-president and chief financial officer since September 2013, would serve as **interim CEO** while continuing as CFO; and that **Harvey C. Jones** — chief executive and executive chairman of **Synopsys**, an entrepreneur and venture investor for three decades — had been appointed the company's **first-ever chair of the board**. The board said it had begun a search for a permanent CEO and would consider internal and external candidates, expressed *\"full confidence\"* in Kress, and kept its third-quarter results date of **Tuesday 17 November**. **Bloomberg** reported that Huang was **ousted by the board** after reports of **three affairs**; **Reuters** reported a relationship with a second employee; the **BBC** reported he has been **summoned to testify before Congress** about his relationship with a woman US officials believe was a Chinese intelligence asset. The market's answer was immediate: the stock fell and dragged the wider market with it, extending a slide that has erased more than **$500 billion** of value since Friday from a company worth about **$4.2 trillion**. **What the board did in one document is what it had refused to do for thirty years.** Nvidia had **eleven** directors including Huang, **no chair**, and **four** directors who had served almost continuously since the 1990s; there was no published succession plan, and attention had fallen on his children **Spencer** and **Madison**, both senior executives. On Sunday the board opened an investigation, retained **Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz**, and said it had *\"no reason to believe\"* that national security or company secrets had been compromised — a statement issued **before** the second relationship was reported. On Wednesday it removed the CEO and installed a chair. It has not yet published the investigation's scope, the recusals, or the report. In Washington the sequence runs the other way: three Republican committee chairs — **Brian Mast**, **John Moolenaar**, **Rick Crawford** — had already requested a closed-door briefing for **18 November** with a subpoena behind the request, and the **Commerce Department** under **Howard Lutnick** is reported to have taken a softer line on Nvidia even as calls grew for tighter controls on AI chip sales to firms like **Megaspeed**. The company's own technology is now generating the commentary: the scandal produced a flood of AI-generated memes, made with the tools it sells.",
  "bullets": [
   "**An interim CEO who is also the CFO concentrates the two functions a crisis needs separated** — Kress holds the finance portfolio and the executive authority simultaneously, with a search of unspecified duration; the direct effect is that the person certifying the numbers is the person answering for the strategy; the compound consequence is that the 17 November results — the first since the resignation — will be read as a verdict on the interim arrangement as much as on the quarter, and a company that cannot separate its books from its leadership has no way to reassure the market except by hiring fast, which is the worst reason to hire",
   "**A governance fix delivered in the same document as the removal is credible only if the sequence is published** — a first-ever chair appointed on the day the founder leaves, an outside law firm retained by the body it must report to, four long-serving directors not yet recused; the direct effect is that the reform reads as an emergency measure rather than a design; the compound consequence is that the investigation's conclusion — whatever it is — will be attributed to the board's need to be seen acting, so the finding is discounted in advance, and the structural repair Nvidia genuinely needs arrives trailing an asterisk it did not have to carry",
   "**The espionage question is unresolved by the resignation and is now a congressional file with a date** — an alleged intelligence relationship inside a Singapore cloud provider in 2023, an FBI warning to lawmakers a year before the public knew, a closed-door briefing set for 18 November, and a subpoena threat; the direct effect is that the most consequential export-control question in the AI economy is examined behind closed doors; the compound consequence is that the answer — was anything compromised — is delivered as a political summary rather than an engineering audit, and the countermeasures the industry needs, from relationship disclosure to security review for staff with foreign commercial exposure, are argued from a record nobody outside the room can read",
   "**Five hundred billion dollars is not the price of a scandal, it is the size of a concentration** — a $4.2 trillion company up more than 470% in five years, inside every index fund and pension, whose stock moved on reporting about a private life; the direct effect is that a governance failure at one firm is a household risk; the compound consequence is that the AI market's single point of trust has been shown to be a single point of failure, and the correction arrives as a general de-rating of the sector rather than a discount to one name — which is how a private matter becomes a public loss",
   "**The person-cult was the product, and it is now the liability** — a founder marketed as the face of an era, a valuation built partly on relationships made *\"because of the trust with Jensen,\"* children in senior roles, and a board that never named a successor; the direct effect is that the asset being removed appears nowhere in the accounts; the compound consequence is that the company must now market a process where it marketed a man — and investors who bought the man will price the process lower until it has a track record, so the trough is set by the calendar of the search rather than by the quality of the business"
  ],
  "verse": "Your wrong understanding however, that material possession and earthly goods do not belong to the assiduousness for the truth of all truth… has, through the belief in a god, tin god or idolised human being, created the senseless attitude in the majority of you Earth-humans… and you are not conscious of the fact that you… have brought upon yourselves great disadvantage in your consciousness-development, as also with regard to your humaneness, your behaviour concerning the love for the next one… the conscientiousness, fairness and righteousness and the bearing of the responsibility in all things.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 28, Verse 351",
  "hinge": "§28:351 names the mechanism precisely — an *idolised human being* produces a wrong understanding that then propagates into fairness, conscientiousness and *the bearing of the responsibility*. Nvidia's board has just done the difficult half. The remaining half is documentary, and every item is cheap. Publish the investigation's scope, its independence and its reporting date, with the long-serving directors recused from the decision. Publish the succession process — the process, not the name — including whether the permanent CEO must be external, and who on the board owns the search. Publish the conflict-of-interest and relationship-disclosure policy with its enforcement record attached, so the standard applied to a vice-president is the standard on the website. And answer Congress in public rather than in a closed room on 18 November: a company whose chips are treated as a strategic asset cannot expect to explain its leadership in private. A board that writes those three pages can be believed whichever way it decided. One that decided at midnight and explained itself in a press release has bought silence, not trust."
